# SyntraLang Implemented Grammar Subset

Status: **implementation-oriented grammar snapshot — pre-alpha**

This grammar describes the syntax currently recognized by the recursive-descent parser at the time of this documentation revision. It is intentionally narrower than the long-term language design. It is not a promise of a stable 1.0 grammar.

The lexer is keyword-light: words such as `fn`, `intent`, `goal`, and `governance` are lexed as identifiers and receive grammatical meaning in the parser.

## Top level

```ebnf
Program          ::= { Declaration } EOF
Declaration      ::= FunctionDecl | GradFunctionDecl | IntentDecl | RuleDecl
FunctionDecl     ::= "fn" Identifier "(" [ ParameterList ] ")" [ "->" TypeRef ] Block
GradFunctionDecl ::= "@" "grad" FunctionDecl
RuleDecl         ::= "rule" Identifier "(" [ ParameterList ] ")" [ "->" TypeRef ] Block
ParameterList    ::= Parameter { "," Parameter }
Parameter        ::= Identifier ":" TypeRef
TypeRef          ::= Identifier [ "<" TypeRef { "," TypeRef } ">" ]
```

## Cognitive declarations

```ebnf
IntentDecl       ::= "intent" Identifier "{" { IntentMember } "}"
IntentMember     ::= IntentStringMember
                   | IntentBlockMember
                   | GoalBlock
                   | EffectsBlock
                   | UncertaintyBlock
                   | GovernanceBlock
IntentStringMember ::= Identifier StringLiteral
IntentBlockMember  ::= Identifier Block

GoalBlock        ::= "goal" Identifier "{" { GoalMember } "}"
GoalMember       ::= "description" StringLiteral
                   | "priority" Expression
                   | "condition" Expression
                   | "target" Expression

EffectsBlock     ::= "effects" "{" [ Identifier { "," Identifier } ] "}"
UncertaintyBlock ::= "uncertainty" "{" { UncertaintyMember } "}"
UncertaintyMember ::= "confidence" Expression
                    | "assumption" StringLiteral
                    | "evidence" Expression
                    | "source" StringLiteral

GovernanceBlock  ::= "governance" "{" { GovernanceMember } "}"
GovernanceMember ::= "requires" Identifier
                   | "approval" Identifier
                   | "policy" StringLiteral
                   | "constraint" Expression
```

## Blocks and statements

```ebnf
Block          ::= "{" { Statement } "}"
Statement      ::= LetBinding
                 | ReturnStatement
                 | BacktrackBlock
                 | Annotation
                 | ExpressionStatement
LetBinding     ::= "let" Identifier [ "=" Expression ] ";"
ReturnStatement ::= "return" Expression ";"
BacktrackBlock ::= "backtrack" Block
Annotation     ::= "::" Identifier [ "(" [ ArgumentList ] ")" ]
ExpressionStatement ::= Expression ";"
```

## Expressions

```ebnf
Expression ::= LogicalOr
LogicalOr  ::= LogicalAnd { "||" LogicalAnd }
LogicalAnd ::= Equality { "&&" Equality }
Equality   ::= Comparison { ("==" | "!=") Comparison }
Comparison ::= Additive { ("<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=") Additive }
Additive   ::= Multiplicative { ("+" | "-") Multiplicative }
Multiplicative ::= Unary { ("*" | "/") Unary }
Unary      ::= ("-" | "!") Unary | Postfix
Postfix    ::= Primary { "(" [ ArgumentList ] ")" }
ArgumentList ::= Expression { "," Expression }

Primary ::= Identifier
          | IntegerLiteral
          | FloatLiteral
          | StringLiteral
          | BooleanLiteral
          | SymbolicExpression
          | SelfModifyExpression
          | Block
SymbolicExpression ::= "symbolic" "(" Identifier ")"
SelfModifyExpression ::= "modify" "(" Identifier "," Expression ")"
```

## Lexical forms

- Identifiers use Unicode XID start/continue rules, with underscore accepted as an initial character.
- Boolean literals are `true` and `false`.
- Decimal integers and decimal floats are supported; numeric separators are accepted only in supported positions.
- `.5` and `1.0` are valid examples; `1.`, `1__2`, `1_.2`, and `1._2` are invalid.
- Strings use double quotes and the lexer recognizes the escapes `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\0`, `\\\\`, `\\"`, and `\\/`.
- Line comments begin with `//`; block comments use `/* ... */`.
- Operators include arithmetic, comparison, logical, arrow, fat-arrow, punctuation, and annotation separators. Not every lexed operator is currently accepted by the parser.

## Deliberate exclusions

This file does not specify imports, modules, match expressions, lambdas, pattern matching, a complete type system, effect clauses on function signatures, or executable runtime semantics. Those appeared in earlier exploratory grammar drafts or remain future design work. They must not be treated as implemented language features.

The parser and tests are the implementation authority. If this grammar and the implementation disagree, record the discrepancy and update both through a reviewed change.
